Subject: [PATCH] constellation: Abort superseded iframe navigations

Dropped in favour of upstream eb511d5c499 (#49426), which aborts the
older pending changes of a navigable when it is navigated again, and
which Servo 0.8.0 includes. The code differs, so equivalence is checked
with this commit's previous Validation (below) on plain upstream
(runbook decision 3). Upstream differs in one respect: it also aborts a
pending change that reloads an entry (from a traversal to a discarded
entry, or from a crash page's replacement), which this commit left
alone. No run of this Validation exercises that case. The specification
sides with neither: while a navigable traverses, its ongoing navigation
is "traversal", and a new navigation of it is ignored
(https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#navigate), where upstream lets
the new navigation win and this commit let both continue. The sync
accepted upstream's behaviour. This commit's test,
cross-document-nav-cross-document-nav-slow-first-response.html, goes
with it; it passes on plain upstream.

Its Validation before this sync: Release build of ohos-main plus this
patch. `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 1 --repeat 10
